431 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 163 0 R
/E (Correlation is a feature selection method that measures the strength of the relationship between each feature and the target variable, usually using a value between -1 and 1. Features with high absolute correlation are considered important because they strongly influence the target, while those with low correlation are often removed. It works best with numerical data and helps quickly identify the most relevant features.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [4]
>>
