442 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 164 0 R
/E (Lasso is an embedded feature selection method that adds a penalty to a model during training, forcing some feature coefficients to become exactly zero. Features with zero coefficients are effectively removed, while the remaining ones are kept as important predictors. This allows Lasso to perform feature selection and model training at the same time, making it powerful for handling high-dimensional data.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [4]
>>
